# Round glmswap: GLM-5.3-Flash's prompt batch with its mixers' Q8_0 projections on the GEMM (GemmFront: a KDA
# mixer's qkv, g_a, beta, g_b and out; a latent mixer's joined stack) from GEMM_FROM = 9 positions a batch, against
# the base 9e7c858b (main before glmswap) whose front runs every projection as q8_0_gemv_mcol in chunks of 8 (each weight read 64 times
# a 512-column batch).
# Decomposition [derived, round report section 1], from glmgroup's runtime values (A6000, place a, G1, P = 4096,
# BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS): a routed layer-batch is front + host union 72.9 + exchange about 1.1 ms (the shadow, 37.8,
# under the union); KDA front 49.9 ms flat, latent 52.5..69.9; 7.2 ms a routed layer-batch outside the leg spans
# (the three dense KDA layers, the head). 31 routed KDA + 3 dense KDA + 11 latent layers.
# H1 (favoured: mcol at m = 8 streams ~195 GB/s): KDA front 49.9 -> 4.6..6.0 ms (GEMM 1.14 GB at 550..700 GB/s,
# the decay pair's 128 mcol launches at their floor, ~1.9 ms non-projection), latent stack 3.3 -> 0.13 ms:
# -1.53..-1.58 s a batch of 512 -> pp512 129..131 (+39..+40 %), pp4096 124..126 (+37..+39 %).
# H3 (glmgemm's: mcol at 550..700 GB/s, ~33 ms fixed): -0.40..-0.59 s a batch -> pp512 100..104 (+8..+12 %),
# pp4096 97..101 (+8..+12 %).
# pp512 is one batch, so the term reads pp4096; pp512 is printed beside it with the same bands.
kind: ab
question: does moving the KDA and latent fronts' projections onto the GEMM cut the prompt batch's card front by
  the H1 term (the one-column gemv at m = 8 streaming near 195 GB/s), or only by H3's?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096, prose prompt (GLM_PROSE from GLM_PROSE_FROM), A6000, plan (a), --ctx 4352, groups of
  one (BLOOMERY_PREFILL_GROUP unset) - (swap - base) / base, paired by round across the two invocations
unit: %
predict: +34..+42
rounds: 2
condition: one hold, two runner invocations back to back, each carrying this card: the base from a tree at
  9e7c858b (/Users/hckim/repo/bloomery-glmswapbase, its own remote dir), then the swap from /Users/hckim/repo/bloomery-glmswap
  (BLOOMERY_REMOTE='~/repo/bloomery-glmswap'), each BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352
