  row's time prompt record names kind=batch and 1 pass at P = 512, 8 at 4096; a row marked [cold], [cpu-busy] or
  [other-busy] is void, and so is a window whose card witness differs between the two invocations. The effect
  predicted (+34 % or more, or H3's +8..+12 %) is far outside the ~5 % a window moves, so pairing across the two
  invocations decides it. Box time ~16..22 min [derived: per invocation two warm-up processes and four rows, six
  loads at 45..75 s, 2 x (5.5 + 45) s of prompt at the base's rate, less at the swap's; plus the two builds]
decide-in: H1 holds: the mcol front was the bound; land the swap, and open the next round on what the front now
  leaves (the latent heads q_b, k_b, v_b and out, 7.41 GB a latent layer-batch on mcol, and the FFNs behind a
  clamped swiglu_quant32 entry), and at G >= 2 the host union, which the KDA layer-batches now wait on
decide-below: under +34 %: if inside H3's +6..+14 %, the 33 ms is fixed non-projection cost - time one batch
  under nsys (the KDA front's launches by kind) before any further GEMM round; if between H3 and H1, name the term
  from the stat prompt lb rows (card_front_ms per kind) before landing
decide-above: past +42 %: the gemv was slower than 195 GB/s or the GEMM faster than 700 GB/s; re-derive the KDA
